{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788281172,"nonce":"AtJLwv75GZZyafIwakLn/b/JqHc=","message":"ACCEPTANCE PROVEN ON A LIVE BENCH — CLOSING. Session 16, 2026-09-01, assembly\n`479e4a1`.\n\nThe headline test, run three times rather than the two the acceptance asks for:\n\n    call 1: bench.id=18838  bill.bench_id=18838  expect_bills=2\n    call 2: bench.id=18839  bill.bench_id=18839  expect_bills=2\n    call 3: bench.id=18840  bill.bench_id=18840  expect_bills=2\n\n    bills -\u003e bills_total 6, benches_with_bills 3\n             18838 -\u003e 2 bills, 18839 -\u003e 2 bills, 18840 -\u003e 2 bills\n\nThree benches, two bills each, never one bench with six. `data.bill.bench_id`\nequals `data.bench.id` on every call, and `expect_bills` reports 2 rather than\nthe old hardcoded 0.\n\n\nWorth recording, because the chaining fix alone did NOT make this acceptance\npass. On the first pass the second call died with:\n\n    world-fixture bench cannot place TableButcher at 126,138 facing North:\n    Butcher table would block butcher table's interaction spot.\n\nSession B correctly gave the `bench` step the placement gate it had never had\n(`3a5ff6c` item 3) and left `FindClearRect` as the SEARCH. `FindClearRect` walks\nthe footprint's own cells and knows no def, so on a map already holding one\nbutcher table it returns the box beside it — whose footprint sits on the first\ntable's interaction cell. The gate then refused, correctly, and the step died on\nits second call. **A validator the site search does not share turns a fixture\ninto a coin flip.**\n\nFixed in `479e4a1`: `FindGatedSite` ring-walks exactly as `FindClearRect` does\nand asks `SiteGate.Check` at each candidate centre — the same routine\n`FixtureSite.Spawn` runs a moment later, so search and placement cannot\ndisagree. Keyed on `PlaceOk` to match FixtureSite, which reports the widget half\nrather than honouring it. `FindClearRect` stays for the zone steps, which have\nno def to gate on.\n\n\n- **`open-letter` — your comment's omission — is fixed with `bill`.** Your\n  reading was right that the body's audit sentence named four steps that CREATE\n  and omitted the one that RESOLVES.\n- **The either/or you called NOT TESTABLE is resolved by keeping the field and\n  making it true**, and `expect_slots_free` went with it — the acceptance names\n  only `expect_bills`, so an implementation could have satisfied the text and\n  still reported 15 free slots on a bench holding two.\n- **The `MaxCount` question is answered as REFUSE**, not silent clear;\n  `clear_bills:true` opts in. `BillStack.AddBill` validates nothing, so the\n  15-bill cap is UI-only and the model would have exceeded it silently.\n- **`BillUtility.MakeNewBill` replaces `new Bill_Production(recipe)`**, so a\n  recipe using an unfinished thing gets the right runtime type.\n- `journal-selftest`, the other route that gained a gate, passes.\n\n\nThe `letter` / `open-letter` chain was not exercised on the bench — the fix is\nidentical in shape to `bill`'s and is proven by reading, not by running. Cheap\nto add: two `letter` steps in one session, then `open-letter`, and check it\nopens the newer one.","files":null}]}